From: zcop <hongson.hn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: include the new port ageing time in switch aggregation

The switch chooses the shortest per-port ageing time before calling the
hardware driver. Publish the new value before notifying it, otherwise an
increase can select the requesting port's old shorter value. Once every
port has been updated, hardware still holds the previous minimum until
another notification arrives. STP topology-change recovery can therefore
leave hardware ageing faster than the bridge requests.

Restore the cached port value if the notifier rejects the update. Keep
the switch-wide minimum across other ports and bridges unchanged.

Signed-off-by: zcop <hongson.hn@gmail.com>

--- a/net/dsa/port.c
+++ b/net/dsa/port.c
@@ -896,17 +896,18 @@
 	unsigned long ageing_jiffies = clock_t_to_jiffies(ageing_clock);
 	unsigned int ageing_time = jiffies_to_msecs(ageing_jiffies);
 	struct dsa_notifier_ageing_time_info info;
+	unsigned int old_ageing_time = dp->ageing_time;
 	int err;
 
 	info.ageing_time = ageing_time;
 
+	/* The switch-wide minimum must include this port's new value. */
+	dp->ageing_time = ageing_time;
 	err = dsa_port_notify(dp, DSA_NOTIFIER_AGEING_TIME, &info);
 	if (err)
-		return err;
-
-	dp->ageing_time = ageing_time;
-
-	return 0;
+		dp->ageing_time = old_ageing_time;
+
+	return err;
 }
 
 int dsa_port_mst_enable(struct dsa_port *dp, bool on,
